the eye. The eye didn't made it, but they've survived it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:44:03-08:00","id":840532,"title":"","content":"I dont know, a bullet on head and a gauru claws on head should be treated in different ways, i still trying to picture a gauru making a sneak attack on a pure in hishu form and it ends only with a stun lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T04:43:08-08:00","id":840556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839621-lethal-damage-on-head?p=840532#post840532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know, a bullet on head and a gauru claws on head should be treated in different ways, i still trying to picture a gauru making a sneak attack on a pure in hishu form and it ends only with a stun lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Pure in Hishu form could react at the very last second - too late to do anything that requires any sort of higher thought than instinct. As they're Uratha themselves, even if that Gauru manages to crunch half of that skull inwards, and the other claw rakes off skin and muscle - that Pure can heal that with no real trouble. All they need to do is Shift - or hope for the best.<br /> <br /> If that Pure has the base level of 7 Health Levels, 7L is going to knock them out. If they have more, then they're not K.O'd, but they're hurting - badly. Sure their body's going into overdrive tro try and heal the damage, but they're pretty much at your mercy. Stunned isn't just &quot;oh, the wind's knocked out of me&quot; easy-as-pie condition. They're basically unable to do anything unless they blow WP - and I'm going to bet that if you can't One-Shot a Werewolf, you better hope you've got the ability to handle the Gauru-splosion the next turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}